---
import { bookingUrl } from '../config';
import ArrowUpRight from './ArrowUpRight.astro';
interface Props { title?: string; emphasis?: string; }
const { title = 'About to make an expensive', emphasis = 'systems decision?' } = Astro.props;
---
<section class="conversation section-dark" aria-labelledby="conversation-title">
  <div class="shell conversation-layout">
    <div><p class="eyebrow">Start with a conversation</p><h2 id="conversation-title" class="display">{title}<br /><em>{emphasis}</em></h2></div>
    <div class="conversation-copy"><p>Before you replace it, let’s figure out what actually needs to change.</p><p>You don’t need to have the problem neatly framed. In fact, that’s often the point.</p><a class="button button--primary" href={bookingUrl('closing')}>Get a second opinion <ArrowUpRight /></a><a class="text-link" href="/contact/">What to bring to the conversation <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </div>
</section>
